From: Sebastian Andrzej Siewior <bigeasy@linutronix.de>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2015 14:26:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 230/328] block/mq: do not invoke preempt_disable()
Origin: https://git.kernel.org/cgit/linux/kernel/git/rt/linux-stable-rt.git/commit?id=28c0bffaa61940b2873bb6a483bbb38c3f90a6ba

preempt_disable() and get_cpu() don't play well together with the sleeping
locks it tries to allocate later.
It seems to be enough to replace it with get_cpu_light() and migrate_disable().

Signed-off-by: Sebastian Andrzej Siewior <bigeasy@linutronix.de>
---
 block/blk-mq.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/block/blk-mq.c b/block/blk-mq.c
index 553360f66944..a037182067f2 100644
--- a/block/blk-mq.c
+++ b/block/blk-mq.c
@@ -1592,14 +1592,14 @@ static void __blk_mq_delay_run_hw_queue(struct blk_mq_hw_ctx *hctx, bool async,
 		return;
 
 	if (!async && !(hctx->flags & BLK_MQ_F_BLOCKING)) {
-		int cpu = get_cpu();
+		int cpu = get_cpu_light();
 		if (cpumask_test_cpu(cpu, hctx->cpumask)) {
 			__blk_mq_run_hw_queue(hctx);
-			put_cpu();
+			put_cpu_light();
 			return;
 		}
 
-		put_cpu();
+		put_cpu_light();
 	}
 
 	kblockd_mod_delayed_work_on(blk_mq_hctx_next_cpu(hctx), &hctx->run_work,
-- 
2.47.3

